      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bonanza was established in 1888 following the discovery of gilsonite, a rare and shiny natural asphalt substance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonanza%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Bonanza comes from the Spanish term for a rich mineral strike, reflecting the optimism of early prospectors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonanza%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early encounters with gilsonite occurred in 1868 when local Native Americans gave the material to a blacksmith who mistook it for coal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bonanza_utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bonanza is located on the Colorado Plateau, an area known for oil drilling and extraction from oil shale deposits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonanza%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Uintah Railway once supported the local mining industry before the line was abandoned in 1939.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
